exports[`Phase 6 graph-aware prose surfaces (all flags on) > seed phase6-on-1 produces stable graph-aware output 1`] = `
{
  "phenomenonNotes": [
    "Everything landing or leaving passes decontamination cycles measured in shifts, not minutes. Unsettled: Are the microbes a medical resource, industrial hazard, or protected environmental evidence? The destabilization centers on Gomeisa Waypoint-895 III: Metabolite bioprospectors license microbial chemistry for pharmaceutical export — except that the license terms assume the biosphere is passive, and the assays keep suggesting otherwise. A petri array glows faint colors that were not in last season's catalog.",
    "Docking, launch, and local prices surge around celebrated safe windows. No one has settled who controls the forecast that decides when the festival begins. The destabilization centers on Gomeisa Waypoint-895 III: Window-festival concessioners run the market stalls, berth fees, and lodging surge each safe window, and the trouble is that their leases price in a festival calendar the forecast board can quietly move. Officials sell civic unity while stranded crews allege the exit window was quietly narrowed.",
    "Transits through the trojan point run on shepherd-posted lanes that shift with every nudge campaign. Crews still ask whose nudge campaign perturbed the camp orbits, and was the drift a side effect or a strategy. The destabilization centers on Gomeisa Waypoint-895 III: Swarm shepherds nudge commercially useful rocks toward the processing camps, though every nudge changes trajectories other shepherds already sold. The registrar's chart room papers over three walls, and none of the walls agree.",
  ],
  "settlementTagHooks": [
    "Plague/Biosafety Fear is what visitors notice first; survival priority was assigned by a list nobody trusts. The crisis around stolen medical supplies keeps deep-space platform politics under stress. Privately, the medical stockpile was traded for route access. Whoever runs the civilian colony sets the terms here.",
    "Medical Triage State is the surface story, but Anti-Corporate Commune shows who benefits from the tension: the public story hides a working political break with corporate control. Coordination drift across the swarm makes refugee dormitory the choke point everyone fights over. Privately, the site is a military listening post. Whoever runs the civilian colony sets the terms here.",
  ],
  "settlementWhyHere": [
    "There is something rare in this volume, and Gomeisa Waypoint-895 III Habitat 55 is the answer to it.",
    "Gomeisa Waypoint-895 Hub maintains its footprint on the ground beneath it. Gomeisa Waypoint-895 Hub stays because the yield outweighs everything that wants it gone.",
  ],
}
`;

